# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[dawdle]]; to [[waste time]]; to [[procrastinate]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:loiter|Thesaurus:procrastinate}}
#* {{RQ:Stevenson Treasure Island|passage=It is something to have been an old soldier, but more still to have been a doctor. There is no time to '''dilly-dally''' in our work.}}
#* {{RQ:Tarkington Gentleman|passage=“I wouldn't '''dilly-dally''' long if I were you,” said Harkless, and his advice seemed good to the shell-men.}}
#* {{RQ:London War of the Classes|passage=It likewise manifests the frankness of men who do not '''dilly-dally''' with terms, but who say what they mean, and who mean to settle down to a long, hard fight.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Jason Bailey|title=‘Basic Instinct’ at 30: A Time Capsule That Can Still Offend|work=The New York Times|date=2022-03-20|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2022/03/20/movies/basic-instinct-sharon-stone.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=No one can accuse the filmmakers of '''dillydallying'''; no sooner have the opening credits ended than we’re watching, via a mirrored ceiling, a couple writhing naked in coital ecstasy.}}

